{
  "title": "The Promised Neverland",
  "description": "Emma, Norman and Ray are the brightest kids at the Grace Field House orphanage. And under the care of the woman they refer to as “Mom,” all the kids have enjoyed a comfortable life. Good food, clean clothes and the perfect environment to learn—what more could an orphan ask for? One day, though, Emma and Norman uncover the dark truth of the outside world they are forbidden from seeing. \n\n(Source: VIZ Media) \n\n*Note: Nominated to the 22nd, 23rd, and 25th Annual Tezuka Osamu Cultural Prize.*\n\nStatus: completed\nTags: Action, Adventure, Caretaker, Childcare, Childhood Friends, Confinement, Cultivation, Dark Fantasy, Dead Friend, Determined Protagonist, Drama, Ensemble Cast, Fantasy, Female Protagonist, Future, Gore, Guardian Relationship, Horror, Human In Monster Nonhuman Environment, Human Livestock, Liar, Male Demographic with Female Lead, Male Protagonist, Manipulation, Murder, Mystery, Orphanage, Philosophy, Psychological, Ranked by Test Scores, Red-Haired Female Lead, Rules, Sci-Fi, Secrets, Shounen, Smart Female Lead, Strategic Minds, Strong Female Lead, Supernatural, Thriller, Time Skip, Tomboyish Female Lead, Travel, Wall, White/Silver-Haired Character, Young Female Lead, Young Male Lead, Adapted to Anime, Adapted to Live Action, Adapted to Movie, Adapted to Novel, Athletic Female Lead, Award Winning, Award-Nominated Work, Battles, Body Horror, Child Protagonist, Children, Coming of Age, Countryside, Demon King, Demon World, Depression, Emotionally Strong Female Lead, Escape, Family, Family Drama, Female Empowerment, Female Lead, Flashbacks, Found Family, Friendship, Genius, Genius Character, Genius Female Lead, Genius Male Lead, Genius Protagonist, Gods, Heterosexual, Hot-Blooded Female Lead, Hot-Blooded Protagonist, Human Experiment, Human In Monster Demon Environment, Important Non-Romantic Relationship, Impulsive Female Lead, Injury, Isolated Location, Isolated Society, Lies, Male Lead, Manipulative Antagonists, Mind Games, Monsters, 